From 8c66d5c71ea9f9b0b40cd4971958042a30588ebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:49:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): sweep XY arcs exactly in the column engine, not as
 inscribed chords

The program sim's column engine cut each XY arc as chords drawn inside
the arc (chord_tol = cell/4). On a convex corner the arc's centre is the
part's corner, so the chords brought the simulated tool up to one
sagitta closer to the part than the real G2/G3. The issue's L-block
contour clipped one column 0.088 mm inside the riser's corner, and the
height verdict read that as a 10 mm gouge, so the post gate refused a
correct program. On a concave corner the same chords stopped a sagitta
short of the wall and hid a real gouge.

New stock_sim::dexel_arc: disc, ball, cone and bull atoms swept along
the true circle. The per-column reach window is closed-form. The bottom
is exact for discs and level arcs, and helical non-disc arcs are split
at their curvature bends and searched by golden section (real
evaluations only, so it never cuts past the tool). Arc end discs are
judged too. XZ/YZ arcs keep their chords. The gouge verdict is
unchanged.

Tests: the L-block repro over MCP (contour_arc_sim), an exact-reach and
dense-scan check per atom, the issue's column, and planted convex and
concave gouges (arc_sweep). stock_sim's chord law is rewritten to the
exact law. Bull column/field parity on the helix arc is bounded by the
field's own chord error, because the field engine still chords (follow-up).

Fixes #402

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
